# COULD I HAVE THIS DANCE – Anne Murray
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
{ns}
{define: D/A base-fret 1 frets x 0 4 2 3 2} 
{define: E7 base-fret 1 frets 0 2 0 1 0 0} 
{define: E7-full base-fret 1 frets 0 2 2 1 3 0} 
{define: EC# base-fret 1 frets 0 2 2 1 2 0} 
{t: COULD I HAVE THIS DANCE – Anne Murray}
{st: (Holyfield/House)}
{artist: Anne Murray}
{composer: Holyfield; House}


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2wagjpWtRII  (Capo 0)

TIP:  You can play a regular (D) instead of the (D/A) but all you do is add your pinky to the 4th string/4th fret and the chord is only played in the intro and outro.

TIP:  The (E7-full) {EC#) (E) in the final chorus is easy to play.  (E7-full) is just (E) with pinky added to 2nd string/3rd fret.  To get to (EC#) just slide the pinky down one fret, and lift off to get to (E).  If it doesn't transpose correctly just play the transposed root cord.

TIP:  Not too fast.  
 
    
